From e12ed8684fee32b20b632349436a52708fec4ffe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:29:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.5.0: Network Diagnostics - tcpdump on Network Tools
 + MCP active-diagnostics tier

Part A (both images): a "Packet Capture" tab on the Network Tools page.
RTCONFIG_TCPDUMP=y (config_base) packages /usr/sbin/tcpdump. New page
Main_PacketCapture_Content.asp + menuTree tab post to a NEW bounded CGI
do_reaper_pcap_cgi (httpd, #ifdef RTCONFIG_TCPDUMP): argv-based tcpdump via _eval
(NEVER a shell), packet-count + alarm(duration) caps, snaplen, strict-charset BPF
filter split into argv tokens, real-interface check (if_nametoindex). Deliberately
does NOT reuse the stock SystemCmd path (its char-whitelist rejects BPF chars and
it is unbounded). Output = decoded text summary shown on the page.

Part B (MCP image only, #ifdef RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP): an active-diagnostics tier in
rmcpd - net_ping / net_traceroute / net_dns_lookup / net_netstat - so the armed AI
Advisor can isolate router vs client vs ISP vs WAN. Per-session opt-in: a new
off-by-default "Allow network diagnostics" checkbox on the Advisor arm card writes
diag=1 into the session file; rmcpd reads it (g_diag), advertises the tier in
tools/list and permits tools/call ONLY when consented. Each probe: argv-exec via
_eval (no shell), single-flight lock, alarm timeout, output cap, syslog audit line.
Targets validated + resolved, and RFC1918 space that is NOT the router's own LAN is
rejected (no internal-network sweeping). net_bufferbloat deferred (needs a bounded
load generator). Advisor promise reworded (RADV_04) to state diagnostics honestly.

i18n: 9 new dict keys (NetworkTools_PktCap*, RADV_73/74) + reworded RADV_04, all 25
dicts in lockstep. noMCP image: Part A present, Part B compiled out. Metal test owed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
